CALL newPutForth(180, 1, 'Voting rights are already robust in this country. The push to \'expand\' them is really about removing every safeguard — ID requirements, signature verification, witness requirements — that exists to make sure the vote is secure and one person equals one vote.');
CALL newPutForth(181, 1, 'Every \'voting rights\' proposal from the left is designed to make it easier to commit fraud and harder to detect it. No ID required. No signature match. No witness. Mail-in voting for everyone. This isn\'t about rights — it\'s about tilting the field.');
CALL newPutForth(183, 1, 'Mail-in voting at scale is an invitation to fraud, harvesting, and coercion. When you vote in person with an ID, you know the vote came from you. When ballots get mailed out to old addresses, to people who\'ve moved or died — the chain of custody is broken.');
CALL newPutForth(439, 1, 'Democrats weaponize the filibuster for years, then discover it\'s an abomination the moment they hold the majority. The rule didn\'t change. Their interest in it changed because their interest in power changed. That\'s the whole story.');
CALL newPutForth(440, 1, 'Win elections. Pass your policies through normal order. If the rules of the Constitution aren\'t working for you, maybe the problem is your policies, not the rules. Conservatives don\'t get to gerrymander away the Constitution — neither do Democrats.');
CALL newPutForth(770, 1, 'One person, one vote — that\'s the irreducible principle of democratic legitimacy. Any system that gives some votes more weight than others, regardless of the rationale, is a departure from that principle that requires extraordinary justification.');
CALL newPutForth(777, 1, 'When you commit a crime, especially a violent one, you\'ve forfeited your claim to full membership in the civic community. Losing the right to vote while incarcerated is a measured consequence — not a lifetime bar for most offenses.');
CALL newPutForth(1365, 1, 'SB 202 modernized Georgia\'s election law. It expanded early voting on weekends — something not previously guaranteed. It added drop boxes that didn\'t exist before. It requires ID for absentee voting, just like in-person voting. That\'s election integrity, not suppression.');
CALL newPutForth(1374, 1, 'Corporations making public statements about election law while bankrolling the politicians who pass it is the definition of virtue signaling. It costs them nothing and buys them goodwill on the left. It means nothing and they know it.');
CALL newPutForth(1378, 1, 'Georgia has good, fair election laws. They\'re reasonable about access and serious about integrity. The claim that they\'re \'voter suppression\' is a coordinated lie designed to put political pressure on Georgia Republicans. It worked on some corporations. It shouldn\'t work on voters.');
CALL newPutForth(1463, 1, 'Democrats win the popular vote for president but underperform in the Senate and Electoral College — the systems that actually determine governance and judicial appointments. The answer to that is winning more Senate seats, not restructuring institutions because you\'re losing them.');




